# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Maximum Independent Set problem {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Maximum Independent Set {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Maximum Independent Set (MIS) problem is a fundamental challenge in combinatorial optimization.\n"
"Formally, given a graph $G(V, E)$, the goal is to find the largest subset of vertices $V_I \\subset V$ such that no two vertices in $V_I$ are connected by an edge, as in $\\nexists (u, v) \\in E : v \\in V_I \\wedge u \\in V_I$.\n"
"Each vertex is assigned a binary decision variable $x_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, and a constraint $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ is introduced for every edge, ensuring that at most one endpoint of each edge is selected.\n"
"The problem can thus be stated as the following maximization problem:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x_i} \\sum_{i \\in V} x_i \\qquad\\text{(find the largest set)}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\quad x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\quad \\forall (u, v) \\in E.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah Maximum Independent Set (MIS) merupakan cabaran asas dalam pengoptimuman kombinatorik.\n"
"Secara formal, diberikan graf $G(V, E)$, matlamatnya adalah untuk mencari subset bucu terbesar $V_I \\subset V$ sedemikian rupa sehingga tiada dua bucu dalam $V_I$ disambungkan oleh tepi, seperti dalam $\\nexists (u, v) \\in E : v \\in V_I \\wedge u \\in V_I$.\n"
"Setiap bucu diberikan pemboleh ubah keputusan binari $x_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, dan kekangan $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ diperkenalkan untuk setiap tepi, memastikan bahawa paling banyak satu hujung bagi setiap tepi dipilih.\n"
"Masalah ini dengan itu boleh dinyatakan sebagai masalah pemaksimuman berikut:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x_i} \\sum_{i \\in V} x_i \\qquad\\text{(cari set terbesar)}\\\\\n"
"\\text{dengan syarat} \\quad x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\quad \\forall (u, v) \\in E.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MIS has a wide range of practical applications. In wireless network planning, an independent set corresponds to a group of transmitters that can all broadcast simultaneously without mutual interference. In scheduling, it models the largest collection of tasks that can execute concurrently given pairwise resource conflicts. In computational biology, it captures sets of mutually non-interacting proteins in a network.\n"
msgstr "MIS mempunyai pelbagai aplikasi praktikal. Dalam perancangan rangkaian wayarles, set bebas sepadan dengan sekumpulan pemancar yang semuanya boleh menyiar secara serentak tanpa gangguan sesama sendiri. Dalam penjadualan, ia memodelkan kumpulan tugas terbesar yang boleh dilaksanakan serentak memandangkan konflik sumber berpasangan. Dalam biologi pengkomputeran, ia menangkap set protein yang tidak saling berinteraksi dalam suatu rangkaian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Despite its intuitive formulation, MIS is NP-hard, and even for graphs with a few hundred nodes specific instances become difficult to solve exactly or heuristically [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
"The problem also gives rise to sparse constraint structures that are well suited for hardware implementations of quantum optimization, making it an attractive benchmark for near-term quantum devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun perumusannya intuitif, MIS adalah NP-hard, dan bagi graf dengan beberapa ratus nod, contoh tertentu menjadi sukar untuk diselesaikan secara tepat atau secara heuristik [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
"Masalah ini juga menghasilkan struktur kekangan jarang yang sangat sesuai untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan pengoptimuman kuantum, menjadikannya penanda aras yang menarik untuk peranti kuantum jangka pendek.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Aqarios Constrained Quantum Optimizer {#aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer}"
msgstr "Aqarios Constrained Quantum Optimizer {#aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The standard approach to embedding a constrained binary problem into quantum optimization transforms the model into an unconstrained format by adding penalty terms: each violated constraint $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ contributes $2 x_u x_v$ to the minimization objective $-\\sum_i x_i$. This is handled automatically by the Constrained Quantum Optimizer Qiskit Function.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan standard untuk membenamkan masalah binari terkekang ke dalam pengoptimuman kuantum mengubah model tersebut menjadi format tanpa kekangan dengan menambah terma penalti: setiap kekangan yang dilanggar $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ menyumbang $2 x_u x_v$ kepada objektif peminimuman $-\\sum_i x_i$. Ini dikendalikan secara automatik oleh Constrained Quantum Optimizer Qiskit Function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond this standard transformation, the optimizer identifies **cliques** in the constraint graph. A clique is a set of nodes $V_C$ where every pair of nodes shares an edge. As a consequence, the $\\binom{|V_C|}{2}$ pairwise constraints $x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\;\\forall (u,v) \\in E_C$ can be replaced by a single, tighter constraint $\\sum_{i \\in V_C} x_i \\leq 1$. Introducing a slack variable $y$ turns this into an equality $\\sum_i x_i + y = 1$, which takes the form of a one-hot constraint that can be enforced directly in QAOA using **XY-mixers** [\\[3\\]](#references). This reduces the search space and avoids the need for penalty terms for those constraints, improving solution quality.\n"
msgstr "Selain transformasi standard ini, pengoptimum mengenal pasti **klik (cliques)** dalam graf kekangan. Klik ialah set nod $V_C$ di mana setiap pasangan nod berkongsi tepi. Akibatnya, $\\binom{|V_C|}{2}$ kekangan berpasangan $x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\;\\forall (u,v) \\in E_C$ boleh digantikan dengan satu kekangan tunggal yang lebih ketat $\\sum_{i \\in V_C} x_i \\leq 1$. Memperkenalkan pemboleh ubah kendur $y$ mengubah ini menjadi persamaan $\\sum_i x_i + y = 1$, yang mengambil bentuk kekangan one-hot yang boleh dikuatkuasakan secara langsung dalam QAOA menggunakan **XY-mixers** [\\[3\\]](#references). Ini mengurangkan ruang carian dan mengelakkan keperluan terma penalti untuk kekangan tersebut, meningkatkan kualiti penyelesaian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additionally, variables connected to only a single neighbor are called **pendant** nodes and are fixed deterministically by the algorithm before quantum execution, further reducing the effective problem size.\n"
msgstr "Selain itu, pemboleh ubah yang disambungkan kepada hanya satu jiran dipanggil nod **pendant** dan ditetapkan secara deterministik oleh algoritma sebelum pelaksanaan kuantum, seterusnya mengurangkan saiz masalah yang efektif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Constrained Quantum Optimizer employs an **iterative warm-starting** approach compatible with XY-mixers [\\[1\\]](#references), which progressively narrows the search space by biasing the quantum state distribution towards promising solution regions across iterations. This enables the use of **fixed-angle QAOA parameters**, eliminating the need for variational parameter training. The total quantum resource requirements are governed solely by the number of warm-start iterations, which means the quantum cost straightforward to control.\n"
msgstr "Constrained Quantum Optimizer menggunakan pendekatan **warm-starting berulang** yang serasi dengan XY-mixers [\\[1\\]](#references), yang secara beransur-ansur mengecilkan ruang carian dengan memberi bias kepada taburan keadaan kuantum ke arah kawasan penyelesaian yang menjanjikan merentasi iterasi. Ini membolehkan penggunaan **parameter QAOA sudut tetap (fixed-angle)**, menghapuskan keperluan latihan parameter variasi. Keperluan sumber kuantum keseluruhan dikawal semata-mata oleh bilangan iterasi warm-start, yang bermakna kos kuantum mudah dikawal.\n"

